{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For managing acid reflux, focus on low-acid and alkaline foods. Good choices include fruits like bananas, melons (watermelon, cantaloupe, honeydew), and apples. Pears, guava, papaya, figs, and pomegranate are also generally well-tolerated, while berries can be consumed in moderation.\n\nMost green vegetables are beneficial, such as spinach, broccoli, green beans, celery, cauliflower, and lettuce. Root vegetables like carrots, sweet potatoes, and beets are also helpful. High-fiber, whole grains like oatmeal, brown rice, and whole-grain breads can help absorb stomach acid. Other good grains include barley, quinoa, and couscous.\n\nOpt for lean proteins like skinless chicken breast, fish, turkey, and extra-lean ground beef, as well as egg whites and tofu. Low-fat or fat-free dairy products such as yogurt, low-fat milk, feta or goat cheese, and fat-free cream cheese are recommended. Almonds, chia seeds, pumpkin seeds, flax seeds, and sesame seeds can also be included. Additionally, ginger (in moderation), fennel, and vegetable broth are beneficial. Staying hydrated with water is also important.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0042-37-07571:2": 0.9990792274475098, "clueweb22-en0021-44-05185:6": 0.997731626033783, "clueweb22-en0018-80-17587:11": 0.9975409507751465, "clueweb22-en0005-41-09262:15": 0.9973226189613342, "clueweb22-en0023-31-01763:3": 0.9969127178192139, "clueweb22-en0002-93-16983:2": 0.996839165687561, "clueweb22-en0017-00-06735:4": 0.996572732925415, "clueweb22-en0018-80-17587:9": 0.9965583682060242, "clueweb22-en0018-87-10874:14": 0.9964589476585388, "clueweb22-en0018-80-17587:10": 0.9963066577911377, "clueweb22-en0030-41-12104:10": 0.9961574673652649, "clueweb22-en0027-11-19840:5": 0.9961495399475098, "clueweb22-en0038-83-05173:5": 0.9960013031959534, "clueweb22-en0002-93-16983:1": 0.9959968328475952, "cluew