{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For stomach acid reflux, focusing on alkaline, low-fat, and high-fiber foods can help alleviate symptoms.\n\nExcellent choices include:\n*   **Fruits:** Bananas, melons (watermelon, cantaloupe, honeydew), and apples are often recommended due to their low acidity or alkaline properties.\n*   **Vegetables:** Green vegetables like asparagus, broccoli, spinach, kale, lettuce, celery, and carrots are naturally low in fat and sugar, helping to reduce stomach acid. Root vegetables like sweet potatoes and potatoes are also beneficial.\n*   **Grains:** High-fiber whole grains such as oatmeal, brown rice, whole-grain breads, couscous, and quinoa can absorb stomach acid and promote better digestion.\n*   **Lean Proteins:** Chicken, turkey, fish, tofu, and egg whites are good low-fat protein options that are easier to digest.\n*   **Other helpful foods:** Ginger, fennel, and fat-free yogurt can also aid in soothing the stomach.\n\nRemember to avoid high-fat foods, spicy foods, citrus fruits, tomatoes, and raw onions, as these can often trigger or worsen acid reflux.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0009-09-00824:3": 0.996729850769043, "clueweb22-en0024-83-01996:17": 0.9962060451507568, "clueweb22-en0018-87-10874:14": 0.9956934452056885, "clueweb22-en0005-41-09262:15": 0.9954633116722107, "clueweb22-en0044-72-05971:1": 0.9931600093841553, "clueweb22-en0002-93-16983:2": 0.9929976463317871, "clueweb22-en0000-61-09646:7": 0.9922682642936707, "clueweb22-en0011-63-17217:7": 0.9922009110450745, "clueweb22-en0039-15-05920:14": 0.9918553829193115, "clueweb22-en0009-09-00824:2": 0.9907972812652588}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0009-09-00824:3": 0.996729850769043, "clueweb22-en0024-83-01996:17": 0.9962060451507568, "clueweb22-en0004-73-09989:16": 0.9958491325378418, "clueweb22-en0018-87-10874:14": 0.9956934452056885,