{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To help manage your acid reflux, consider adopting several lifestyle and dietary strategies.\n\nRegarding your eating habits, it's beneficial to eat smaller, more frequent meals rather than large ones, and avoid overeating. Chew your food thoroughly and eat slowly. A crucial step is to avoid eating for at least three hours before lying down or going to bed. After meals, remain upright (sitting or standing) for at least 45-60 minutes, and avoid vigorous exercise immediately afterward. Elevating the head of your bed can also help prevent reflux while sleeping.\n\nDietary wise, prioritize a low-fat diet rich in whole foods, vegetables, fruits, and whole grains. Opt for healthy complex carbohydrates and increase your fiber intake. Reduce or eliminate common trigger foods like fatty, sugary, or processed items, carbonated beverages, alcohol, and caffeine. Keeping a food journal can help you identify your personal triggers.\n\nBeyond diet, maintaining a healthy weight and incorporating regular physical activity can significantly reduce symptoms. Stress reduction techniques like meditation or deep breathing, and ensuring you get enough sleep, are also beneficial. If you smoke, quitting can greatly improve symptoms.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0027-58-19039:6": 0.9424898028373718, "clueweb22-en0037-74-14945:10": 0.8731949925422668, "clueweb22-en0039-92-15038:12": 0.8649526238441467, "clueweb22-en0021-74-19197:6": 0.8584749102592468, "clueweb22-en0002-38-10912:5": 0.8583984375, "clueweb22-en0028-64-19668:2": 0.8458192944526672, "clueweb22-en0045-80-00595:13": 0.8206283450126648, "clueweb22-en0046-54-03909:9": 0.8173685073852539, "clueweb22-en0026-96-04891:1": 0.8165855407714844, "clueweb22-en0045-95-01180:2": 0.8094860315322876, "clueweb22-en0009-95-06055:9": 0.8039219975471497, "clueweb22-en0013-99-00483:3": 0.80211871862