{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Yes, your approaching deadline could definitely be related to your acid reflux. As we discussed earlier, stress can worsen acid reflux symptoms for some people.\n\nRegarding over-the-counter (OTC) medications, there are several options available to help manage acid reflux:\n\n1.  **Antacids:** These provide quick, short-term relief by neutralizing stomach acid. Common examples include Tums, Rolaids, Mylanta, Maalox, and Gaviscon.\n2.  **H2-receptor blockers (H2 blockers):** These work by reducing the amount of acid your stomach produces, offering longer relief than antacids. OTC examples include cimetidine (Tagamet HB), famotidine (Pepcid AC), and nizatidine (Axid AR).\n3.  **Proton Pump Inhibitors (PPIs):** These are stronger and block acid production more effectively, also allowing damaged esophageal tissue to heal. OTC PPIs include omeprazole (Prilosec OTC) and lansoprazole (Prevacid 24 HR).\n\nWhile these OTC medications can provide relief, it's always best to consult your doctor if your symptoms are persistent or severe, to ensure proper diagnosis and treatment.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0002-04-09789:3": 0.994526207447052, "clueweb22-en0039-92-15038:12": 0.9432330131530762, "clueweb22-en0016-97-03528:3": 0.9323940873146057, "clueweb22-en0026-80-18810:6": 0.9163756370544434, "clueweb22-en0005-31-05925:5": 0.8884838819503784, "clueweb22-en0027-47-12028:2": 0.8765193223953247}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0002-04-09789:3": 0.994526207447052, "clueweb22-en0017-96-03792:10": 0.9614062309265137, "clueweb22-en0041-97-07392:7": 0.9478048086166382, "clueweb22-en0039-92-15038:12": 0.9432330131530762, "clueweb22-en0016-97-03528:3": 0.9323940873146057, "clueweb22-en0019-30-04613:4": 0.9315044283866882, "clueweb22-en0006-20-05889:3": 0.9246161580085754, "clueweb22-en0015-45-13434:4": 0.92139708