{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-1_3", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To improve the taste of your coffee and make it gentler on your stomach, consider a few approaches.\n\nFirst, regularly cleaning your coffee machine is crucial (Passage 4, 6, 9, 20). Built-up coffee oils can cause a stale and bitter taste. Running a vinegar solution through it monthly can remove residue.\n\nFor the taste itself, adding a pinch of salt can significantly help (Passage 5, 8, 9, 11, 20). Salt counteracts bitterness, enhances the coffee's natural flavor, and, importantly, can help fight acid reflux and heartburn (Passage 8, 20). You can add a dash to your brewed coffee or even a teaspoon to six tablespoons of coffee grounds before brewing.\n\nIf bitterness is a main concern, full-fat milk or cream can reduce it effectively (Passage 4, 5, 7, 11). For a different flavor, you could try a drop of vanilla essence or a dash of ground cinnamon (Passage 1, 14).\n\nTo specifically address your mild acid reflux, cold brew coffee is an excellent option (Passage 15, 19). It has lower acidity because fewer acidic compounds are extracted, making it much gentler on sensitive stomachs. Another method to neutralize acidity is to add a small amount of baking soda (around 1/4 teaspoon per cup) or use almond milk, which is alkaline (Passage 13).", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0014-27-03756:2": 0.9457916021347046, "clueweb22-en0005-49-10565:6": 0.9136409163475037, "clueweb22-en0029-18-03900:2": 0.9136318564414978, "clueweb22-en0015-02-10471:6": 0.9046496152877808, "clueweb22-en0029-18-03900:3": 0.9023763537406921, "clueweb22-en0035-41-14346:10": 0.8972483277320862, "clueweb22-en0039-92-06362:14": 0.8934555053710938, "clueweb22-en0029-18-03900:1": 0.8596234321594238, "clueweb22-en0014-61-17727:9": 0.8425352573394775, "clueweb22-en0015-09-14580:9": 0.8403418064117432, "clueweb22-en0026-11-03407:8": 0.832315981388092, "clueweb22