{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-1_12", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The impact of roasting on coffee taste, particularly concerning acidity and stomach gentleness, is significant. For someone who occasionally experiences mild acid reflux and prefers beverages that are gentle on the stomach, a darker roast is generally the best option.\n\nThe longer and darker a coffee is roasted, the lower its acidity will be. Light roasts are typically the most acidic, while medium roasts offer a more balanced acidity. Dark roasts, on the other hand, are known for having lower acid levels, making them gentler on the stomach.\n\nThis is because darker roasts contain higher levels of N-methylpyridium (NMP), a chemical produced during the roasting process that can block the production of stomach acid, thus reducing irritation. Additionally, longer roasting times can destroy oils in the beans that might otherwise contribute to acid buildup. Studies have also shown that dark roast coffee can reduce gastric acid secretion, further contributing to its stomach-friendly nature.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0041-83-12827:18": 0.49602195620536804, "clueweb22-en0005-30-03345:11": 0.4423663020133972, "clueweb22-en0015-13-06066:4": 0.32227206230163574, "clueweb22-en0041-15-00331:6": 0.3169615566730499, "clueweb22-en0007-44-13475:5": 0.2926604747772217, "clueweb22-en0015-41-16401:2": 0.2845880091190338, "clueweb22-en0017-76-18714:13": 0.27946507930755615, "clueweb22-en0015-13-06066:1": 0.27230462431907654}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0041-83-12827:18": 0.49602195620536804, "clueweb22-en0005-30-03345:11": 0.4423663020133972, "clueweb22-en0030-53-00764:5": 0.429971843957901, "clueweb22-en0003-60-13479:7": 0.39566999673843384, "clueweb22-en0030-53-00764:4": 0.37583035230636597, "clueweb22-en0044-33-07902:5": 0.35262224078178406, "clueweb22-en0041-83-12827:7": 0.34570562839508057, "clueweb