{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-2_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "After a race in New York City, you have several excellent options to relax and unwind.\n\nIf you're near the Central Park Marathon finish line, several hotels offer quiet and comfortable spaces. The Hotel Beacon on the Upper West Side has rooms with living areas and kitchenettes, plus ample lobbies for relaxing. The La Quinta by Wyndham New York City Central Park and Hudson New York also provide comfortable, relaxed environments. For a more luxurious recovery, the Mandarin Oriental New York, located near Central Park, boasts a full-service spa, massage rooms, and saunas with a relaxation lounge. The Hotel Lucerne also features an on-site fitness center and spa.\n\nBeyond hotels, New York City offers numerous tranquil spots. Central Park itself is an obvious choice for unwinding, as is Bryant Park, a quiet oasis in Midtown Manhattan perfect for sunbathing or reading. For a truly serene experience, head to the New York Botanical Garden in the Bronx, a 250-acre oasis with 50 unique gardens, offering peace and quiet. You might also find calm at the New York Public Library's reading rooms or in Midtown's small pocket parks like Paley Park or Greenacre Park.\n\nIf you prefer a different kind of relaxation, consider the beaches. Manhattan Beach and Brighton Beach in Brooklyn offer more open spaces and a relaxed atmosphere, a good change from the city's bustle.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0025-53-15295:3": 0.9634510278701782, "clueweb22-en0025-53-15295:4": 0.9430104494094849, "clueweb22-en0020-79-05412:5": 0.8987815976142883, "clueweb22-en0034-85-01089:6": 0.8708227872848511, "clueweb22-en0025-53-15295:12": 0.8599277138710022, "clueweb22-en0025-53-15295:6": 0.8475598096847534, "clueweb22-en0042-53-06895:5": 0.826310396194458, "clueweb22-en0004-96-03746:0": 0.8096725940704346, "clueweb22-en0020-99-01942:4": 0.8093929886817