{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "It's understandable to want to improve your skin's appearance without relying solely on serums. For addressing dark spots, uneven skin tone, and large pores with minimal downtime, several other topical solutions are available.\n\nYou can consider **creams** containing ingredients like retinol, niacinamide (Vitamin B3), vitamin C, or collagen. Retinol creams, for example, promote skin cell turnover, unclog pores, and reduce the appearance of dark spots and large pores. Niacinamide in creams can also enhance the skin's protective barrier, reduce blemishes, large pores, and hyperpigmentation. Vitamin C day creams can brighten dark spots and even skin tone.\n\n**Cleansers** and **face washes** formulated with ingredients like charcoal, witch hazel, or Vitamin C can help remove impurities, tighten pores, and brighten your complexion.\n\n**Leave-on exfoliants** such as those containing Beta Hydroxy Acid (BHA, like salicylic acid) or Alpha Hydroxy Acid (AHA, like glycolic acid) are effective for unclogging and diminishing enlarged pores, smoothing texture, and evening out skin tone. LHA (Lipo-Hydroxy Acid) also provides micro-exfoliation to tighten pores.\n\nAdditionally, specialized **moisturizers** and **lotions** are available that target dark spots and uneven tone, often containing brightening ingredients. Don't forget the importance of **sunscreen** with zinc oxide, as sun protection is crucial in preventing new dark spots and protecting your skin.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0028-21-15069:8": 0.796239972114563, "clueweb22-en0025-54-13891:5": 0.7803018093109131, "clueweb22-en0034-93-12196:6": 0.7658931612968445, "clueweb22-en0022-61-11497:5": 0.7414405941963196, "clueweb22-en0016-40-15259:7": 0.733853280544281, "clueweb22-en0043-24-07735:11": 0.7105486392974854, "clueweb22-en0015-41-01032:3": 0.7078128457069397, "cl