{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "CO2 laser treatment works by using concentrated beams of light, generated by electricity passing through a gas-filled tube. This light targets water molecules in your skin, vaporizing surface skin cells of the epidermis and making way for fresh, new skin. Simultaneously, the laser penetrates the deeper dermis layer, where it heats the tissue and stimulates the production of new collagen and elastin fibers. This process helps to firm and smooth your skin over time.\n\nThere are two main types: fully ablative and fractional. Fully ablative CO2 lasers remove the entire superficial skin layer in the treated area. Fractional CO2 lasers, on the other hand, deliver the light in a pixelated pattern, creating thousands of tiny shafts of light that penetrate the deeper layers. In both cases, the body's natural healing process is promoted, pushing out old, damaged skin and replacing it with new, healthier tissue, leading to tighter, smoother skin with reduced lines, wrinkles, scars, and pigmentation. The heat also helps to shrink existing collagen.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:1": 0.9988401532173157, "clueweb22-en0025-02-00163:1": 0.9712554216384888, "clueweb22-en0040-62-12136:1": 0.9357315897941589, "clueweb22-en0031-65-04139:2": 0.9272724986076355, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:10": 0.9174416065216064, "clueweb22-en0032-14-04213:8": 0.8533777594566345, "clueweb22-en0002-32-13360:17": 0.8283112645149231}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:1": 0.9988401532173157, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:13": 0.9831081032752991, "clueweb22-en0025-02-00163:1": 0.9712554216384888, "clueweb22-en0008-96-16607:2": 0.9463271498680115, "clueweb22-en0037-37-03816:4": 0.9376450777053833, "clueweb22-en0040-62-12136:1": 0.9357315897941589, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:2": 0.92844158411026, "clueweb22-en0031-65