{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_12", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "After microneedling, it's essential to be very gentle with your skin. You should avoid using your face wash containing salicylic acid immediately after the treatment. Products with salicylic acid, along with other strong exfoliating acids like AHAs (alpha hydroxy acids) and BHAs (beta hydroxy acids), can cause irritation, potentially harm the skin, or slow down the regeneration process due to the temporary micro-channels created. It's recommended to use gentle, mild, and fragrance-free cleansers for at least a week, or wait at least three days before reintroducing active ingredients like salicylic acid.\n\nRegarding your oily scalp and hair products, it's advised to refrain from your regular hair care routines after microneedling, especially if your scalp was treated, as the procedure creates tiny wounds. Allow your skin and scalp to heal properly. It's also recommended to avoid direct high heat, such as from blow dryers or very hot showers, in the treated areas.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:11": 0.8808438181877136, "clueweb22-en0001-02-00582:9": 0.8151851296424866, "clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:10": 0.7479522824287415, "clueweb22-en0001-02-00582:10": 0.7298820614814758, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:1": 0.6941631436347961, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:2": 0.6807834506034851, "clueweb22-en0009-89-01915:7": 0.6362844705581665, "clueweb22-en0033-70-02855:6": 0.6240315437316895, "clueweb22-en0030-73-16433:6": 0.5750718116760254}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:11": 0.8808438181877136, "clueweb22-en0001-02-00582:9": 0.8151851296424866, "clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:13": 0.7545871734619141, "clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:10": 0.7479522824287415, "clueweb22-en0001-02-00582:10": 0.7298820614814758, "clueweb22-en0033-70-02855:7": 0.7177735567092896, "clueweb22-en0033-70-02855:8": 0.69759