{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The Pomodoro Technique is a time management method that uses a timer to break down work into focused intervals, typically 25 minutes in length, separated by short breaks. Here's how it generally works:\n1.  **Choose a single task:** Select one specific task you want to focus on. The core idea is to dedicate your attention solely to this task during the work interval.\n2.  **Set a timer:** Set a timer for 25 minutes. This 25-minute period is called a \"Pomodoro.\"\n3.  **Work with focus:** For the next 25 minutes, concentrate entirely on your chosen task. If other thoughts or distractions arise, make a quick note of them and immediately redirect your focus back to the task.\n4.  **Take a short break:** When the 25-minute timer rings, take a short 5-minute break. Use this time to step away from your work, stretch, or briefly relax.\n5.  **Repeat:** After your 5-minute break, start another 25-minute Pomodoro session on your task.\n6.  **Longer break:** After completing four Pomodoro sessions, take a longer break of 20-30 minutes to rest and recharge before starting a new cycle.\n\nThis structured approach helps manage your attention, makes tasks feel less overwhelming, and can prevent the urge to switch between tasks without completion.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0001-66-11662:19": 0.4307188391685486, "clueweb22-en0001-30-00712:21": 0.27487483620643616, "clueweb22-en0026-06-01592:6": 0.6293796896934509, "clueweb22-en0004-59-16742:12": 0.48363128304481506, "clueweb22-en0012-51-00120:12": 0.3992123007774353, "clueweb22-en0001-66-11662:18": 0.35166269540786743, "clueweb22-en0018-44-00826:12": 0.3455849587917328, "clueweb22-en0027-14-08624:10": 0.2974970042705536, "clueweb22-en0001-49-04668:16": 0.2821824252605438, "clueweb22-en0009-59-12729:4": 0.27580952644348145}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en