{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-2_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "That's a great approach for a hobby! To learn tattooing self-taught, focus on building your skills systematically.\n\nFirst, hone your artistic abilities. Practice drawing and shading extensively on paper with pencils or paint, experimenting with various strokes to prepare for different tattooing styles.\n\nNext, get hands-on with your tattoo machine and supplies. A good way to practice is on fruits like apples or pears, as their skin texture is similar to human skin. This helps you understand needle depth; if the fruit is damaged, you're likely going too deep. When using your machine, aim to insert the needle at a 45-degree angle to ensure the ink stays, and learn to vary pressure for different shades. Pay close attention to needle protrusion, ensuring it's not more than 1mm, and experiment with machine speed for soft versus bold shades. Steady your movements by supporting your hand on the practice surface.\n\nCrucially, maintain strict hygiene. Prepare a clean, flat, well-lit workspace by thoroughly washing and disinfecting the surface, then lay down paper towels. Always properly dispose of all needles to prevent infection. Mastering these techniques and safety practices on practice materials will build a strong foundation for your tattooing hobby.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0007-52-05511:16": 0.5500880479812622, "clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:13": 0.3186087906360626, "clueweb22-en0007-71-06134:8": 0.28378763794898987, "clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:11": 0.27678751945495605, "clueweb22-en0019-99-06369:1": 0.253033846616745}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0007-52-05511:16": 0.5500880479812622, "clueweb22-en0007-71-06134:7": 0.5426350235939026, "clueweb22-en0028-52-08765:6": 0.3680228292942047, "clueweb22-en0032-30-09102:8": 0.3367357850074768, "clueweb22-en0024-15-17670:2": 0.3297870457172394, "cl