{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-2_3", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "That's great you're ready to apply ink! Beyond your tattoo machine and fake skin, here's a list of essential supplies to get started safely and effectively as a hobbyist:\n\n**For Power & Operation:**\n*   **Power supply, clip cord, and foot pedal:** These are crucial to power and control your tattoo machine.\n\n**For Ink Application:**\n*   **Sterile tattoo needles:** You'll need a variety of sizes for different line work and shading.\n*   **Tattoo ink:** Start with high-quality black ink, and perhaps a few basic colors.\n*   **Ink caps/cups and an ink cup holder:** To hold your ink securely during the process.\n*   **Grips/tubes/tips:** Disposable options are highly recommended for hygiene.\n*   **Small parts:** O-rings, rubber bands, and grommets are often needed for machine setup and stability.\n\n**For Hygiene & Safety (Crucial for any tattooing):**\n*   **Disposable gloves:** Always wear fresh gloves to prevent contamination.\n*   **Skin cleanser/disinfectant:** To prepare the skin before tattooing.\n*   **Surface disinfectant and antibacterial soap:** For maintaining a clean workspace and cleaning up.\n*   **Sharps container:** A safe place to dispose of used needles.\n\n**For Aftercare & Prep:**\n*   **Petroleum jelly (Vaseline) or a dedicated tattoo balm:** Used during tattooing for lubrication and for initial aftercare.\n*   **Bandages and medical tape:** To cover the fresh tattoo.\n*   **Transfer paper and a marker pen:** To apply your designs to the skin.\n\nRemember, even as a hobby, strict hygiene is paramount to prevent infections.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0001-91-13299:14": 0.48318567872047424, "clueweb22-en0020-24-16033:20": 0.44497716426849365, "clueweb22-en0020-24-16033:21": 0.4421866536140442, "clueweb22-en0032-43-06101:5": 0.40664908289909363, "clueweb22-en0030-49-10071:8": 0.39700058102607