{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-2_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "REACH stands for Registration, Evaluation, Authorization and Restriction of Chemicals. It is a comprehensive European Union regulation (EC 1907/2006) that applies throughout the EU, including Germany. Its primary purpose, overseen by the European Chemicals Agency (ECHA), is to protect human health and the environment from the risks posed by chemical substances.\n\nIn the context of tattooing, the EU's Tattoo-REACH regulation came into force on January 4, 2022. This regulation significantly restricts the use of certain tattoo inks by banning around 4,000 chemicals, including common ingredients like isopropanol alcohol, that are deemed \"dangerous substances.\" These substances are restricted due to their potential to cause health issues such as skin allergies, genetic mutations, and cancer. The regulation aims to make tattoos safer, not to ban them entirely. Consequently, many previously available colored tattoo inks are now prohibited, and manufacturers have faced challenges in providing compliant alternatives, which has led to criticism and uncertainty within the tattoo industry in Germany and across Europe.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0000-83-16967:1": 0.5293591022491455, "clueweb22-en0018-61-05246:2": 0.35335516929626465, "clueweb22-en0033-74-18753:1": 0.2809668183326721, "clueweb22-en0018-61-05246:3": 0.22407472133636475, "clueweb22-en0033-74-18753:0": 0.22031165659427643, "clueweb22-en0000-83-16967:2": 0.2181949019432068, "clueweb22-en0018-02-09618:1": 0.17491476237773895, "clueweb22-en0019-01-04994:7": 0.15259458124637604}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0000-83-16967:1": 0.5293591022491455, "clueweb22-en0004-54-09219:6": 0.39577165246009827, "clueweb22-en0018-61-05246:2": 0.35335516929626465, "clueweb22-en0046-30-10934:8": 0.3036136031150818, "clueweb22-en0046-30-10934:7": 0.3018417060