{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Since you're thinking about your pedals, it's good to know there are two main types for mountain bikes: flat (or platform) pedals and clipless (or clip-in) pedals.\n\nGiven your casual riding style on forest trails and rough paths, and your preference for comfort and avoiding DIY complexities, upgrading to higher-quality flat pedals might be a great choice. Unlike basic plastic ones, modern flat pedals are often made from durable materials like aluminum or magnesium. They feature numerous strategically placed metal pins or studs on each side, which provide excellent grip for your feet, especially in wet or muddy conditions common on trails. A wider platform also offers better support and control. Look for models with sealed cartridge bearings, as these keep out water and gunk, reducing the need for maintenance. Flat pedals allow you to use any comfortable shoe, making them versatile and easy to use without learning to clip in and out.\n\nClipless pedals, on the other hand, attach your feet directly to the pedal using special cleats on your shoes, offering greater pedaling efficiency, especially for climbing. However, they require specific shoes and some practice to disengage quickly, which might be less ideal if you prioritize comfort and simplicity over speed.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:4": 0.6322503685951233, "clueweb22-en0025-76-12903:3": 0.6497124433517456, "clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:8": 0.5329952239990234, "clueweb22-en0039-52-09693:5": 0.653433620929718, "clueweb22-en0046-39-18236:16": 0.6193361878395081, "clueweb22-en0037-60-07465:4": 0.5275324583053589}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0036-32-05251:4": 0.6894830465316772, "clueweb22-en0039-52-09693:5": 0.653433620929718, "clueweb22-en0025-76-12903:3": 0.6497124433517456, "clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:4": 0.6322503685951233