{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "When looking for mountain bike flat platform pedals, several key features contribute to performance and comfort.\n\nFirst, consider the **material**. Most durable flat pedals are made from aluminum or magnesium alloy for the body, offering a good balance of strength and weight. The spindle, which is the axle the pedal rotates on, is often made of robust chromoly steel or, for high-end options, titanium.\n\n**Grip** is crucial for mountain biking. Look for pedals with metal traction pins (also called anti-skid pins or studs) that dig into your shoe soles for superior hold, especially in wet or muddy conditions. Many high-quality pedals have replaceable and even adjustable pins, allowing you to customize the grip.\n\nThe **platform size and shape** are also important. A wide platform provides better support for your feet, improving leverage for cornering and pumping, and allowing you to adjust foot placement for better control. Some pedals feature a concave profile, which can offer extra stability and a more \"locked-in\" feel.\n\nFinally, check for **sealed bearings**. These prevent dirt and water from entering the pedal's internal components, ensuring smooth rotation, extending the pedal's lifespan, and reducing the need for frequent maintenance. Many quality pedals are also fully serviceable, meaning bearings and bushings can be replaced over time.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0039-39-12967:3": 0.678178608417511, "clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:8": 0.5338026285171509, "clueweb22-en0025-76-12903:3": 0.48603829741477966, "clueweb22-en0036-51-05870:15": 0.4114910960197449, "clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:9": 0.4045769274234772, "clueweb22-en0028-26-07066:1": 0.3309342861175537, "clueweb22-en0011-06-11770:0": 0.32533398270606995, "clueweb22-en0011-06-11770:2": 0.32016003131866455, "clueweb22-en0030-36-02569:8": 0.3148066997528