{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-trained-MiniLM", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To open your bike chain using a chain breaker tool, follow these steps:\n\n1.  **Position the Chain:** Locate the link you want to break. Your chain tool has two prongs next to a small metal pin. Slide the chain link between these prongs, ensuring it's securely in place and the prongs fit into the gaps on either side of the link. Line up the tool's driving pin with the rivet (the small metal pin) in the center of the chain link.\n2.  **Push the Pin:** Turn the handle on the chain tool clockwise. This will push the rivet out of the link. Continue turning until the rivet is almost completely out of the link, but **do not push it all the way through**. It should be clear of the outer plate but still attached to the inner plate. Pushing it completely out makes reinstallation very difficult.\n3.  **Release and Separate:** Once the pin is mostly out, turn the handle counterclockwise to retract the chain tool's pin. Remove the chain from the tool. Gently wiggle the link back and forth to fully separate the chain at the point where the pin was pushed out.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:2": 0.9640488028526306, "clueweb22-en0022-62-09551:8": 0.9494052529335022, "clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:3": 0.9231864213943481, "clueweb22-en0022-62-09551:9": 0.9140427112579346, "clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:3": 0.905078113079071, "clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:6": 0.8910589218139648}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:2": 0.9640488028526306, "clueweb22-en0022-62-09551:8": 0.9494052529335022, "clueweb22-en0023-31-20248:9": 0.9409701824188232, "clueweb22-en0021-86-13969:6": 0.9347057342529297, "clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:3": 0.9231864213943481, "clueweb22-en0021-86-13969:5": 0.9230859279632568, "clueweb22-en0041-04-13329:3": 0.9206090569496155, "clueweb22-en0022-62-09551:9": 0.9140427112579346, "clueweb22-e